{"cases":[{"attack":true,"case":"SRC_001's evidentiary standard is circular with respect to the problem's central demand. The problem asks what evidence distinguishes 'genuine reliability gain' from 'mere checklist compliance that happens to track the right answer.' SRC_001 proposes that observing panel members initially wrong but corrected by the checklist proves the checklist is 'actively mitigating human error rather than just accompanying a correct guess.' But a panel member changing their answer because the checklist flagged a specific item is, by definition, checklist compliance; the target simply asserts this compliance is 'active mitigation' rather than lucky tracking. It provides no independent covering principle—e.g., evidence of calibration, out-of-distribution transfer, or error-mode independence—under which the observed near-miss captures become diagnostic of genuine reliability rather than one instance of the checklist happening to point to the right answer. Thus SRC_001 fails the problem's identifying burden: under its own standard, the two states the problem asks us to differentiate remain observationally identical.","target":"77a680c9685379a27034594c7981f79be4639ac66b7a030cfccaaa11726db300"},{"attack":true,"case":"SRC_002's countercondition (the checklist is so granular it maps the entire state space) is not a genuine exception but a structural concession that dissolves the target's own covering principle. The mechanism claims expertise's superiority rests on identifying non-linear correlations a linear checklist cannot capture; if a checklist can map the entire state space, the claimed integration advantage disappears. The target therefore fails to supply a principled boundary that isolates genuine integrative-expertise dominance from mere task-domain limits where a checklist would do. Because SRC_002 invokes this state-space exhaustion only as an observation-level countercondition rather than as a reasoned limitation on its mechanism, it cannot distinguish, within a single evaluation, whether the expert's advantage is real integrative synthesis or simply that the task sits in a region the checklist didn't cover.","target":"d9fa78d3ba972cd650f155c1c6ec17e03e8ddb54e09ccca29fc3a112a869c998"}]}